# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-13, R-4, RC-6). L §5.14.2 Takes in the first batch: "A cycle among them (two places
# sweeping into each other in one batch, each arrival keeping labels) breaks where it can: each take is tried with the
# cycle's arrivals as parts of unknown labels, and a take whose outcome is the same under every reading of them ... is
# decided, which breaks the cycle. Otherwise a cycle that holds a plan is refused (RUN-CYCLE, naming the movements) ...
# A cycle of observed rows only is an unknown fact ...: the takes it reaches are undecided, each place holds a hole part
# with its total known (§8.1)".
# Three batched places in a ring of observed rows (r1 konto -> konto2, r2 konto2 -> konto3, r3 konto3 -> konto): one
# cycle of three groups, each place a hole part with its total known (80.00, 60.00, 50.00; scratch/exp6.py); the day
# before, the parts are known (b1's 100.00 carried).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind lots: place PLN min 0
  batched
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order k.batch.day
input bank: observed
place konto: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place konto2: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place konto3: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input b1_day: date
input b1_amt: money PLN
input b2_day: date
input b2_amt: money PLN
input b3_day: date
input b3_amt: money PLN
move b1: transfers
  on b1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b1_amt
move b2: transfers
  on b2_day
  leg cash from world to konto2 amount b2_amt
move b3: transfers
  on b3_day
  leg cash from world to konto3 amount b3_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-01), bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of b1, bal(konto2, 2026-03-01), bal(konto3, 2026-03-01), bal(konto3, 2026-03-01) of b3, bal(konto, 2026-02-28) of b1

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto3] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  b1_day = 2026-02-01
  b1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  b2_day = 2026-02-15
  b2_amt = 50.00 PLN
  b3_day = 2026-02-20
  b3_amt = 40.00 PLN
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-01, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to konto2 amount 30.00 PLN) "r1"
  bank[r2] = (on: 2026-03-01, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto2 to konto3 amount 20.00 PLN) "r2"
  bank[r3] = (on: 2026-03-01, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto3 to konto amount 10.00 PLN) "r3"
=== expect
q: (80.00 PLN, ?"konto: 80.00 PLN may be b1's: which of bank[r1], bank[r2], bank[r3] went first on 2026-03-01?" (konto), 60.00 PLN, 50.00 PLN, ?"konto3: 50.00 PLN may be b3's: which of bank[r1], bank[r2], bank[r3] went first on 2026-03-01?" (konto3), 100.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: b1
  unfulfilled: b2
  unfulfilled: b3
  cut 2026-10-01
